cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this Dortmund IGT focused-ultrasound and synchronized auditory
  masking adaptation, please cite the software as specified below. Separately
  acknowledge the upstream Radboud driver and the auditory masking software by
  Hira Musarrat and Benjamin Kop when applicable.
type: software
title: >-
  Focused Ultrasound Driving System with Synchronized Auditory Masking for Active
  and Sham Entorhinal Cortex Stimulation
authors:
  - family-names: Apochi
    given-names: Obed
    affiliation: Ruhr University Bochum, Germany
    website: https://github.com/Obediko
  - family-names: Axmacher
    given-names: Nikolai
    affiliation: Ruhr University Bochum, Germany
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-22
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22059704
repository-code: https://github.com/Obediko/fus-driving-system-auditory-masking
url: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22059704
abstract: >-
  A research software adaptation integrating reproducible auditory masking,
  fail-closed headphone checks, and active/sham orchestration with an Image
  Guided Therapy D054 focused-ultrasound driving system. The reference protocol
  targets the posterior-medial entorhinal cortex using a 300 kHz carrier, 5 Hz
  pulse repetition frequency, 20 ms pulse duration, and 90 s stimulation.
keywords:
  - transcranial ultrasound stimulation
  - focused ultrasound
  - auditory masking
  - sham stimulation
  - entorhinal cortex
  - neuromodulation
  - research software
